OL,3,AHalf the harvest, twice the bills: how
OL,4,Adrought hit farms
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe hottest summer on record, the
OL,7,Flongest drought, the worst harvest.
OL,8,FWest Country farmers are counting the
OL,9,Fcost of a "terrible summer", as one put
OL,10,Fit.
OL,12,FThe wheat harvest on Charles Day's
OL,13,Ffamily farm in Gloucestershire was cut
OL,14,Fin half. "It's just soul-destroying,"
OL,15,Fhe says.
OL,17,FDairy farmers had to rip open silage
OL,18,Fclamps stored up for the winter to feed
OL,19,Fthe cattle as the grass failed. Sarah
OL,20,FGodwin calculates it cost her family's
OL,21,FWiltshire farm "over #100,000". She
OL,22,Fsays "it's shocking".
OL,23,APub: 07-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB  BusinessC Nat TVF  Nat News
